# consolidated runtime state dir (PATHIA_STATE_DIR, 2026-07-09)
.state/

# alpha_swarm re-fetchable data caches. These are downloaded candles, funding,
# filings and event tables — regenerate by rerunning the hypothesis script that
# built them (W-U1_unlock_backtest.py for the W-U set, and so on). They were
# tracked until 2026-09-01, which put 83MB of throwaway JSON in every clone; the
# three W-U/W-R entries that used to be listed here by name are covered by the
# patterns below. Findings, specs, hypothesis code and *_results.json stay
# tracked — those are the evidence, and test_evidence_doctrine reads them.
research/alpha_swarm/**/*_cache_*.json
research/alpha_swarm/**/*_cache_texts/
research/alpha_swarm/**/*_events.json
research/alpha_swarm/**/*_dataset.json

# Per-IDE agent skill copies, written by the installed caveman plugin. All three
# are byte-for-byte the same 22 files as each other and as the plugin's own
# cache, so tracking them vendored an installed plugin into a trading repo three
# times over. Worse, the plugin rewrites them on session events: on 2026-09-01
# .forge/ and .qwen/ vanished mid-session and showed up as 44 phantom deletions
# in `git status` that nobody had made. They stay on disk, the plugin owns them,
# git does not.
.agents/
.forge/
.qwen/
